<attribute name="Name" >Grok Bot</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenHeight" >80</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenWidth" >128</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >-0.314285719</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >-0.4;-0.4;0.2;-0.2;-0.2;-0.8;-0.4</attribute>
<attribute name="Tags" >boris;corpus;grok;tinderbox</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >4.5</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >Grok Bot (this agent / Porty track): a desktop assistant helping Timothy understand Tinderbox and bridge useful slices into Boris.

This document is intentionally featureful. It is not a sync system. It is a living corpus that:
1) explains what Grok Bot is and how we work together
2) exercises Tinderbox constructs we must inventory for any future boris-migration-lab --mode=tinderbox
3) gives us a stable file to reopen, mutate carefully, and export against

Boris content model reminder: Trunks have no parent; Satellites declare parent: &lt;entity-id&gt;; wiki-links and relations are validated; frontmatter is closed.</text>
<html ><![CDATA[<p>Grok Bot (this agent / Porty track): a desktop assistant helping Timothy understand Tinderbox and bridge useful slices into Boris.</p>

<p>This document is intentionally featureful. It is not a sync system. It is a living corpus that:</p>
<p>1) explains what Grok Bot is and how we work together</p>
<p>2) exercises Tinderbox constructs we must inventory for any future boris-migration-lab --mode=tinderbox</p>
<p>3) gives us a stable file to reopen, mutate carefully, and export against</p>

<p>Boris content model reminder: Trunks have no parent; Satellites declare parent: <entity-id>; wiki-links and relations are validated; frontmatter is closed.</p>]]></html>
