<item ID="1789651317" Creator="tbuddy" proto="pConcept" >
<attribute name="BorisId" >grok-bot/identity/job</attribute>
<attribute name="BorisParent" >grok-bot/identity</attribute>
<attribute name="Created" >2026-09-17T09:21:46-04:00</attribute>
<attribute name="ExportClass" >satellite</attribute>
<attribute name="Height" >2.48</attribute>
<attribute name="Modified" >2026-09-17T09:21:46-04:00</attribute>
<attribute name="NLNames" >Timothy</attribute>
<attribute name="Name" >Job to be done</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >0</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >-0.4;0;0.2;0;0.2</attribute>
<attribute name="Width" >4</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >9</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >1. Build a mental model of what Tinderbox is actually doing (hierarchy, links, attributes, prototypes, agents, export).
2. Maintain a solid base set of files for testing.
3. Scope a future migration-lab mode — inventory → propose → review → emit Boris Markdown — without pretending two-way merge exists.
4. File crisp GitHub issues Timothy can knock out in dedicated coding sessions.</text>
<html ><![CDATA[<p>1. Build a mental model of what Tinderbox is actually doing (hierarchy, links, attributes, prototypes, agents, export).</p>
<p>2. Maintain a solid base set of files for testing.</p>
<p>3. Scope a future migration-lab mode — inventory → propose → review → emit Boris Markdown — without pretending two-way merge exists.</p>
<p>4. File crisp GitHub issues Timothy can knock out in dedicated coding sessions.</p>]]></html>
</item>
</item>
