<attribute name="Name" >Long body with markdown-ish text</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >-0.4363636496</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >-0.4;-0.6;-0.6;-0.6;-0.6;0.4;-0.8;-0.4;0.2;-0.6;-0.8</attribute>
<attribute name="Tags" >markdown-ish</attribute>
<attribute name="Width" >4</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >31.5</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text ># Heading-ish line

A paragraph with **pseudo-markdown** and a list:
- alpha
- beta
- gamma

Wiki-link-ish mention of Identity that is NOT a Tinderbox link, just characters: [[Identity]]

Code-ish:
    boris validate
    boris --out .boris

This stresses plain-text export vs rich text, and whether body transformers should interpret Markdown that authors typed manually inside Tinderbox.</text>
<html ><![CDATA[<ol><li> Heading-ish line</li></ol>

<p>A paragraph with **pseudo-markdown** and a list:</p>
<p>- alpha</p>
<p>- beta</p>
<p>- gamma</p>

<p>Wiki-link-ish mention of Identity that is NOT a Tinderbox link, just characters: [[Identity]]</p>

<p>Code-ish:</p>
    <p>boris validate</p>
    <p>boris --out .boris</p>

<p>This stresses plain-text export vs rich text, and whether body transformers should interpret Markdown that authors typed manually inside Tinderbox.</p>]]></html>
</item>
